    {
      "id": "5ef43ba4-d6c8-482f-a908-40b1426a19e3",
      "phaseId": "0e4c21e5-1cf7-4c0a-a00e-76ffbef60703",
      "number": 395,
      "shortId": "BLRSH",
      "priority": 7,
      "shortName": "context-menus-declared-on-the",
      "title": "Context menus declared on the widget — a ContextMenu value, a host sink, and one generalised action",
      "status": "in-progress",
      "description": "**Part 2 of 2. `P084(F004)/T394` (the event vocabulary + framework-owned routing) is DONE and driven\nby Antonio in the app, 2026-08-06.**\n\n# ⚠️ THE API WAS RE-DECIDED BY ANTONIO 2026-08-07 — this section wins over everything below it\n\nThe first implementation grew `path` / `target` / `about` / `alter_menus` / `MenuPath::declare` /\n`MenuRow::at`. **Every one of those existed only so a *different* component could add a row to your\nmenu**, and that single requirement reshaped the whole API. Antonio: *\"the API is too verbose and\nerror prone\"*, *\"why a function that return vec?? still the same as before.. WHY?? i want simple\nAPIs\"*. All of it is dropped.\n\n## The decided model\n\n**A menu is a value, built where the data is, attached by putting it in the tree.**\n\n```rust\nlet menu = Menu::new(\"Pane\", \"What you can do with this pane\")\n    .name(\"workspaces.pane\")                       // OPTIONAL — see below\n    .child(MenuItem::new(\"Rename\").on_click(move || rename(id)))\n    .child(MenuItem::new(\"Close\").danger(true).on_click(move || close(id)));\n\nRow::new()\n    .child(Label::new(&pane.name))\n    .child(menu);        // ← attached here; shown when this row is right-clicked\n```\n\n- **No path, no target, no `about`, no registry lookup, no id string anywhere.** `id` is captured by\n  the closure, because the menu is built in the loop that is already drawing that row from that\n  pane's data. That is the whole point of declaring it on the widget.\n- **`Menu::new(title, description)`** — the description is what makes a menu self-documenting rather\n  than needing a separate declaration step.\n- **`.name(\"workspaces.pane\")` is OPTIONAL** and is the *only* thing left of the contribution\n  design: it gives other components a handle to add rows to. A menu without a name is closed and\n  needs nothing.\n- **Reuse is a factory, not a borrow.** `.child(&ws_menu)` cannot work — children are owned\n  (`Box<dyn Component>`) and a menu holds closures, which are not `Clone`. Use\n  `let ws_menu = || Menu::new(..)…;` then `.child(ws_menu())`. Agreed with Antonio.\n- **Consequence of dropping `about`, recorded so nobody is surprised:** a row contributed by another\n  component to a *named* menu has no per-row payload, so it acts on app state (the focused pane,\n  the selected row) rather than on the row the menu was opened for. If that turns out to matter it\n  is one additive builder later — do not pre-build it.\n\n## Then, in this task, after the API above is built\n\n- **Menu rows composed of children**: `MenuItem` content becomes `.child(Icon::new(..))`,\n  `.child(Label::new(..))` instead of a label+icon record. This is the settled widget architecture\n  (\"a hand-drawn leaf is a refactor target\") and it is a **rewrite of `ContextMenu`'s paint and\n  hit-test**, not an added method — the rows are drawn by hand today. Antonio wants to see it on\n  screen before it is called done.\n- Antonio, same message: *\"we need to also rewrite that button to be a ViewNode at the end but first\n  handle this\"* — the composed-content refactor for `Button`, **after** the menu work.\n\n# Already built (2026-08-06/07, uncommitted, all green)\n\n- `MenuItem::new(label).on_click(f)` + `.icon/.key/.shortcut/.danger/.enabled`; `MenuEntry` kept as\n  an alias so existing callers compile.\n- `ContextMenu::child(item)`, `show_at(point)`, `show_under(bounds)` — both `show*` public, the\n  declaration implemented in terms of them, and **the framework picks the anchor** (cursor for a\n  right-click, under the widget for a keyboard trigger) so an author never chooses one. `show_under`\n  hangs the panel off the widget's bottom edge (it used to centre *on* the widget, covering the row\n  the menu was about).\n- `Base::context_menu` + `EventExt::context_menu(closure)` — universal, like `nav_key`.\n- `heca-grid-ui/src/menu.rs`: `install_menu_sink` (the `install_frame_request` pattern), bubbling to\n  the nearest declaring ancestor, `open_for_focused` for the keyboard trigger.\n- Router: an **unclaimed** `RightClick` opens the nearest declared menu, so a widget answering its\n  own right-click still wins.\n- App: the sink is installed at startup and queues (`AppState::pending_menus`); the event loop\n  drains it once a frame into a layer via `chrome::overlay::present_menu`, sharing\n  `insert_menu_layer` with `open_dropdown`. `ContextMenu::after_select` lets the host take the layer\n  down so an item stays a plain closure.\n- `heca-grid-ui/tests/context_menu_declaration.rs` — 8 tests, one per settled rule.\n\n**To rework against the decided model:** `ContextMenu::path()` / `.target()` and\n`overlay::merge_contributions` were built for the dropped design — `path`/`target` become\n`Menu::name()`, and merging keys off the name.\n\n# What this still deletes (unchanged)\n\n`context_path` (providers/workspaces/mod.rs:311), the `menu(id, builder)` registrations (:300), the\n`MENU_PANE`/`MENU_COLUMN`/`MENU_WORKSPACE` constants (:1263), `open_row_context_menu` (mouse.rs:156)\nand its position archaeology, and the `nav_key`-or-no-menu trap.\n\n# Triggers, anchors, bubbling (settled, unchanged)\n\n| Trigger | Target | Anchor |\n|---|---|---|\n| `Event::RightClick` | the widget under the pointer | the pointer |\n| the `open_context_menu` action (`prefix+>`, `Shift+F10`, `Menu`) | the focused widget | under the widget |\n\nBoth bubble to the **nearest** ancestor holding a menu; menus are never merged; nothing declared ⇒\nnothing opens (a host that wants \"right-click empty space\" puts one on the root).\n`open_context_menu` is **generalised, not duplicated**: it stops meaning \"the focused pane's menu\"\nand starts meaning \"the focused widget's, bubbling\"; `Shift+F10` and `Menu` become extra bindings on\nthe **same** catalogued action, deliberately not a `[keys.widgets]` entry.\n\n# Verification\n\nHeadless tests per rule, but the real check is Antonio right-clicking a pane, a column, a workspace,\nempty sidebar space and a plugin widget, plus `prefix+>` and `Shift+F10`. **Do not claim it works.**",
